  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nCloud cover has increased across the region early this morning.\nEnough lift and moisture should be present to form some spotty\nshowers across NE PA northeastward into the Western Catskills as\nwe head toward sunrise. Just how fast these clouds clear out\nwill determine how unstable the environment will become. \n\nModeling has trended faster with the main round of showers and\nthunderstorms. This activity should move into our region early\nin the afternoon then exit by early evening. This limits the\nwindow for instability compared to previous model cycles. Still,\nsome instability coupled with modest shear should allow for \nstrong to severe thunderstorms. The highest chances continue to \nbe in NE PA with more uncertainity the further north you go. The\nmain concern looks to be from gusty to locally damaging winds. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nAdditional showers and clouds should linger through Wednesday \nwith an upper level low passing to our north. High pressure then\nbuilds into the region for the remainder of the week with a\ncooler refreshing airmass. This will give way to slowly\nincreasing heat and humidity. Our next chance for showers and \nthunderstorms will be ahead of a cold front Monday.",
